==Enemy==
Cumulus Gallus is a Chickful A given the Behemoth treatment, gaining draconic wings, red eyes, and bolts of lighting that it can call from the sky. Its newfound attributes include lower range, immunity to slow/weaken, very high health, faster and more powerful attacks and 150% strengthen at 33% HP.

==Strategy==
Cumulus Gallus' immunity to Slow and Weaken renders [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]], [[Otaku Geek Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hacker Geek Cat]] and [[Driller Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Driller Cat]] useless against it, however, it can still be frozen using cats like [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]] and [[Sweet Love Mekako (Uber Rare Cat)|Sweet Love Mekako]]. Attackers like [[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Awakened Urs]] can also exploit their range advantage, as Cumulus Gallus is more of a midranger than a backliner. As for meatshields, [[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]] is able to survive a Strengthened hit from Cumulus Gallus at a minimum of level 43, though fast meatshields such as [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] may be a better choice in [[Empress' Excavation 3]] due to the restrictions. [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] and [[Lifeguard Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Gelato Bro Cats]] have the range to serve as weaker but safer attackers than [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], which can be used to hurt Cumulus Gallus and survive an un-Strengthened hit, but won't survive long past that.

